  <div class="prose">
    <p>I'm an engineer who started out in electronics, fell for signal and image processing, and ended up spending two years teaching neural networks to find people in thermal images taken from drones. These days I build applied AI systems at <strong>Ascendion</strong> in Bengaluru.</p>
    <p>What I care about most is understanding <em>why</em> a model works, not only that it does. I like small, efficient architectures, honest evaluations, and measuring what matters instead of what's easy to measure. Outside of work I read about cosmology and spacetime, which is a nice reminder that there are harder problems than class imbalance.</p>
    <p>This site is where I write down what I learn. Some of it is polished, a lot of it is notes. If something here was useful, or wrong, I'd love to hear about it.</p>

